__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ddflow/index.db*

# `uv.lock` is COMMITTED, deliberately, and used to be listed here.
#
# It does not affect users: `uvx ddflow-mcp` and `pip install ddflow-mcp` resolve from
# the published metadata and never read this file. It affects CI and contributors,
# which is exactly where it matters — every workflow runs `uv run pytest`, and without
# a lock that resolves whatever is newest on the day. "Green yesterday, red today, same
# commit" is not a failure anyone can debug from the diff.
#
# The dependency it pins is also the one this project has already been bitten by: for
# as long as Jinja2 was undeclared, the suite ran a different template engine depending
# on whose interpreter it was (docs/BACKLOG.md B154).

# ddflow task worktrees (git worktrees; never commit them)
.ddflow-worktrees/

# Machine-local ddflow configuration: YOUR services (reviewer endpoints, API-key variable
# names) and machine sizing (test workers). ddflow reads these beside .ddflow/config.toml;
# they are never committed, so the repository stays generic.
.ddflow/reviewers.toml
.ddflow/gates.toml
# roborev's agent/model/reasoning (decision D-roborev-local); git carries .roborev.toml.example.
.roborev.toml

